### Content summary

- **Purpose:** AI judgment for **sense of place** on KS desktop interfaces (`Msm`, `museum-studio`, `forge-app-shell`) — complements `DET.APP.PERSISTENT_CHROME`, breadcrumbs, chrome boundary, landmarks.
- **Passing / failing signals:** Stable `data-shell-region` chrome, breadcrumbs, `ks-workspace-lens__segment--active`, `ks-wizard-flow__session-item` + `aria-current`, `data-route-contract="persistent-shell"`; failures include chrome rebuilds, generic “Workspace” titles, competing nav rails.
- **Before example:** Tablist in header, generic “Workspace” `h2`, no trail or session marker.
- **After example:** Persistent shell, Lens segments, session rail, breadcrumb, route `h1`, `forge-card` step copy.
- **Evidence / remediation:** PDCA capture + five-step fix list, including deterministic promotion when tab disorientation repeats.

### Real KS class names used

`Msm`, `data-ks-type="desktop-interface"`, `data-persistent-chrome`, `data-shell-regions`, `data-route-contract`, `nav-section-label`, `ks-workspace-lens*` (from `css/workspace-lens.css`), `ks-wizard-flow__session-list` / `__session-item`, `forge-card`, `card-label`, `forge-support`, `breadcrumb`, Bootstrap `btn` variants — aligned with the `DET.APP.PERSISTENT_CHROME` auditor fixture.

